.TH EZBIND 1 "2026-10-24" "ezbind 0.1.0-dev B2" "User Commands"
.\" CHG-015 split-command interface; targeted implementation verification complete.
.SH NAME
ezbind \- prepare PDFs for folded-folio home bookbinding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ezbind text
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.I INPUT.pdf
.I OUTPUT.pdf
.PP
.B ezbind cover
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.B --front
.I FRONT.svg
.B --back
.I BACK.svg
.I OUTPUT.pdf
.PP
.B ezbind --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ezbind
provides separate text and cover commands. The text command reads a local input
PDF and writes a duplex folded-folio arrangement. Each output sheet has two
finished-page positions on each side. The nominal folio assignment is
front-left 4, front-right 1, back-left 2, and back-right 3. Incomplete final
folios are padded with blank logical pages.
.PP
The cover command reads front and back SVG files and writes a separate cover
PDF without opening a text-block PDF. Each invocation produces one output.
There is no combined mode and no compatibility alias for the former
.BR --cover-*
options; users needing both outputs run the commands separately.
.PP
Top-level help lists the commands; each command has command-specific help and
usage. Help works on its own. The text command takes exactly INPUT.pdf and
OUTPUT.pdf. The cover command takes exactly one positional output and requires
.B --front
and
.BR --back .
Options may be interspersed with positional paths;
.B --
ends option parsing. Examples prefer options first. Supply values as separate
arguments, such as
.BR --sheet a4 ,
not
.BR --sheet=a4 .
Attached short values and grouped short flags are not supported. Each command
rejects its own normalized source/destination path collisions.
.PP
Each command replaces its single destination without prompting only after
successful generation. The previously verified B2 interface predates this
split-command update. Targeted CHG-015 implementation verification is recorded in
the B2 Test Description; broader B2 acceptance and independent physical review remain pending.
Physical cover cards, adhesive, and fabric remain user-supplied.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help , \-h
Print applicable help without requiring input files and return status 0. Top-level
help lists commands; invoke command-specific help on its own.
.TP
.BR --sheet\~letter | \-s\~letter | --sheet\~a4 | \-s\~a4
Select the physical output sheet. Letter is the default. Output is landscape:
792 x 612 points for Letter and approximately 841.89 x 595.28 points for A4.
.TP
.BR --grid , \-g
Add light-gray vector grid lines in text-mode margin areas. The default spacing is
5 mm. Grid lines are not added unless this option is selected.
.TP
.B --grid-spacing \fIVALUE\fR, -G \fIVALUE\fR
Set positive grid spacing in \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR; the default is
5 mm. This option does not enable the grid; also supply --grid.
.TP
.BR --margin-top\~VALUE | \-t\~VALUE | --margin-bottom\~VALUE | \-b\~VALUE
Set text-mode top or bottom output clearance. Values require a non-negative
\fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix. Defaults are zero.
.TP
.BR --crop-top\~VALUE | --crop-bottom\~VALUE | --crop-left\~VALUE | --crop-right\~VALUE
Remove text-mode source-page edge distances before placement. Cropping may
remove source content but must leave positive page area. Values require a
non-negative \fBmm\fR, \fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix and default to zero.
Distances are measured from the effective CropBox, falling back to MediaBox;
edge names refer to visual edges after rotation. Auto-crop is not enabled.
.TP
.BR --margin-fore-edge\~VALUE | \-e\~VALUE | --margin-spine\~VALUE | \-i\~VALUE
Set text-mode fore-edge or spine output clearance. The spine is the fold-facing
inner edge; the fore-edge is outer. Values require a non-negative \fBmm\fR,
\fBin\fR, or \fBpt\fR suffix. Both defaults are zero.
.TP
.B --front \fIPATH\fR
Required front SVG artwork for the cover command.
.TP
.B --back \fIPATH\fR
Required back SVG artwork, rendered on the left half of the landscape cover
sheet. The output PDF is the final positional argument. Front artwork is
rendered on the right half; a dashed gray center cut guide is drawn over the
artwork, inset 12 points from the top and bottom edges. Artwork is fitted
proportionally to each half-sheet viewport.
.SH DEFAULT LAYOUT
Text mode uses a landscape Letter or A4 sheet with two finished-page positions
per side. Source pages are fitted uniformly inside the resulting content
rectangle without distortion. Source crop options are applied before this fit.
Aspect-ratio differences may leave additional letterboxing. The optional grid
occupies reserved strips and does not cross source content. A one-page source
produces two physical output sides; source counts are padded to multiples of
four.
.SH OUTPUT AND PHYSICAL WORKFLOW
Print text output duplex using the printer setting appropriate for the selected
paper. Fold each sheet once with the fold toward the spine, keep the generated
folio order, and stack before gluing the spine side. Confirm duplex orientation
with a small asymmetric fixture before committing a valuable book.
.PP
For the cover command, print the separate cover PDF on the selected cardstock
size. The back artwork is on the left and the front artwork is on the right;
cut along the dashed gray center guide so both cut edges face the spine. The
guide is inset 12 points from the sheet edges. Cover artwork is rendered by
librsvg onto a Cairo PDF surface and fitted proportionally to each half-sheet
viewport.
.PP
Each command writes to a sibling temporary file named
DESTINATION.ezbind.tmp before replacement. Do not use these names for source
files or other data, or run concurrent invocations targeting the same
 destination. Each invocation only commits its own output after successful
generation. If both outputs are needed, run two commands. Separate invocations
cannot check cross-invocation path collisions together and are not
transactional. Path checks resolve relative components and symbolic links but
do not identify distinct hard links to the same file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Input PDF error, including unreadable, malformed, or empty input.
.TP
.B 4
Impossible layout.
.TP
.B 5
Output, filesystem, or SVG-rendering error.
.TP
.B 6
Reserved for missing or unusable runtime dependencies by the interface
contract. The current application does not return this status; shared-library
loader failures occur before application error handling.
.TP
.B 10
Unexpected internal processing error.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Usage errors are written to standard error and include the selected command's
usage. Ordinary diagnostics do not include extracted source text, passwords,
or complete PDF content. Success messages identifying written destinations are
printed to standard output.
.SH PDF LIMITATIONS
The qpdf backend preserves visible page content and selectable text for the
implemented folio placement path. Cover artwork is rendered through librsvg
2.58 and Cairo; unsupported SVG features, external resources, and font
availability can affect output and must be validated against representative
artwork. Spine/fabric guides, auto-crop, crop/fold/registration marks, creep,
printer safe-area configuration, and broad document-feature capability
reporting are not yet exposed by this B2 slice. Source-page annotations and
form fields may not follow clipped content.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
ezbind text --sheet a4 --grid book.pdf book-bound.pdf
.fi
.PP
Generate a separate cover sheet:
.PP
.nf
ezbind cover --sheet letter --back back.svg --front front.svg covers.pdf
.fi
.PP
The cover command does not require a text-block PDF:
.PP
.nf
ezbind cover --sheet letter --back back.svg \
  --front front.svg covers.pdf
.fi
.PP
Handle dash-leading positional filenames by ending option parsing:
.PP
.nf
ezbind text --sheet a4 -- -book.pdf -bound.pdf
.fi
.SH CHANGE STATUS
This documentation describes the user-authorized CHG-015 interface. Targeted
implementation verification is complete and recorded in the project test record.
Historical combined-mode results do not verify this interface. Broader B2
acceptance and independent physical review remain pending.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qpdf (1)
